<decision #track.execute-ai-agent-resources-through-eidolon-runtime.generic-runtime apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?01M0QP4KTKXCEQSN5Z070SW66H>
  What runtime executes a resource-backed Agent?
  </?01M0QP4KTKXCEQSN5Z070SW66H>
  <answer (
    <raw-answer ?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY0594>
    The existing Eidolon delegate actor runtime.
    </?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY0594>
    <decision-text ?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY0595>
    Resource Agents SHALL materialize to generic AgentConfig and execute through AgentRegistry, spawnChildExecutionActor, existing provider/tool policies and the Conversation Domain.
    </?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY0595>
    <rationale ?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY0596>
    A resource-specific actor or session path would duplicate the platform and violate the mission boundary.
    </?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY0596>
    <evidence ?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY0597>
    Generic actor runtime integration and recovery tests.
    </?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY0597>
  )>
  <confidence ?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY0598>
  0.99
  </?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY0598>
  <reversibility ?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY0599>
  low
  </?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY0599>
)>

<decision #track.execute-ai-agent-resources-through-eidolon-runtime.freeze-fact apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY059A>
  What must be persisted before workflow Agent dispatch?
  </?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY059A>
  <answer (
    <raw-answer ?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY059B>
    The depa receipt and immutable host execution plan.
    </?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY059B>
    <decision-text ?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY059C>
    WorkflowFactStore SHALL persist a task/effect-bound execution fact before dispatch; recovery SHALL use its frozen generic config without rereading the live package.
    </?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY059C>
    <rationale ?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY059D>
    A digest receipt alone cannot recreate prompt text after the source disappears, while a second registry is unnecessary.
    </?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY059D>
    <evidence ?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY059E>
    Durable effect evidence and source-removal recovery tests.
    </?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY059E>
  )>
  <confidence ?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY059F>
  0.98
  </?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY059F>
  <reversibility ?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY059G>
  moderate
  </?01M0QP4KTMHVFQEFWMKJPY059G>
)>
